WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.310
A seaside town keeps two
records, month by month.

2
00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:07.040
Line one: ice creams sold.

3
00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:10.540
Line two: swimmers rescued by lifeguards.

4
00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:11.600
Watch them.

5
00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:14.820
When ice cream sales climb, rescues climb.

6
00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:17.740
When sales drop, rescues drop too.

7
00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:19.930
So is ice cream to blame?

8
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:22.440
Should the town ban it from the beach?

9
00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:25.560
In this mission, you'll
learn what a correlation is:

10
00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:30.160
an association between two variables,
where neither is manipulated.

11
00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:33.940
You'll plot them on a scatter
diagram, one dot for each case,

12
00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:36.900
and see what a positive
correlation looks like.

13
00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:40.750
Your mission: decide whether
ice cream is really to blame.
